## Founder-effect correction — adoption relevance

The 2026-09-09 `INTENT-0029` correction does **not** change this PR's shared transport/integrity/durable-recovery objective. Those repairs remain dependencies of the founder loop.

It does clarify what should come immediately after safe adoption:

- do not launch another literal morphogenesis/developmental subsystem;
- compose the repaired shared substrate with the persistent Goal Chase;
- treat a durable `CapabilityDeficit` as the trigger for **resourceful capability resolution**;
- search/acquire/adapt existing capabilities, open source, APIs/plugins/services, authorized computer use and small tools before inventing architecture;
- use OMNIMORPH only when organization design is demonstrably the residual bottleneck;
- verify and attach the capability under existing authority, then resume the original goal.

Governing rule: **Preserve the effect. Do not literalize the metaphor.**

All existing #98 blockers and evidence remain unchanged. This comment does not waive the 17 broader Kernel failures, DALEOBANKS offline-isolation blocker, Docker verification, lint debt, independent review, or any no-merge/no-deploy/no-activation restriction.
